Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Causal Time", "GuideTitle",
 CellID->942062912,ExpressionUUID->"a3a3c038-ca24-47b7-9945-83f1c1312fe3"],

Cell["\<\
A time function on a causal graph is a map to the integers that increases \
along every edge. The universal time is the height: the length of the longest \
chain from a source to the event, zero on the sources. Its level sets, the \
slices of the universal foliation, are antichains that partition the events, \
and the slice through an event is the discrete analogue of a simultaneity \
surface. A slice is an inert set head read like a ball, and a random slice is \
its support.\
\>", "GuideAbstract",
 CellID->2001916300,ExpressionUUID->"ef0ab37b-2e0d-4399-8f7e-82603ccbe925"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["", "GuideFunctionsSection",
